// Four equal bars, 3:2, from the designer's image (1440 by 960 pixels).
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Asexual spectrum flag"
  designer "theflagarchive (Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2020-07-25"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20210814095909/https://theflagarchive.tumblr.com/post/624655680467599360/asexual-spectrum-flag-while-i-like-the-asexual"
  note "Designer's own post on the Tumblr blog Flag Archive (theflagarchive), read from the Wayback snapshot above; the page's metadata dates it 2020-07-25. It says any ace-spec person can use the flag and gives the meanings: dark blue, the community, its history and solidarity; purple, asexuality of all kinds; 'red' (the third bar, drawn pink), self determination and pride; cream, diversity in experiences and types of attraction. It gives no hex values or proportion. Wiki pages are reported to name the blog's author Potion, which the post does not show."
  note "The colors were read near the hoist edge of the post's flag image, which has text across its bars (the 500 by 333 copy Tumblr serves of a 1440 by 960 original, fetched from Tumblr's media server): #151847, #7657ae, #da92b4, #ffeced. The bars are equal, and the proportion 3:2 is the image's."
  note "The Fandom wiki's file page is reported to credit a kyanitedragon post (624812264044789760) instead; it was not reached. The theflagarchive post is two days older. The same blog's aromantic spectrum flag was made as its pair."
}
palette {
  dark-blue "#151847"
  purple "#7657ae"
  pink "#da92b4"
  cream "#ffeced"
}
proportion hoist=2 fly=3

bars dark-blue purple pink cream
